  "claim_boundary": "A fixed exploratory depth atlas on the already exposed 292-item T9/T10 population. It compares raw Unicode emoji surfaces with official Unicode names and literal U+ codepoint strings in the same nine model/tokenizer cells, carriers, and distances used by T10. It may describe where an item-specific glyph/name retrieval advantage appears, peaks, or disappears across normalized decoder depth. It is not a new item holdout or an independent replication and cannot establish rendered-glyph perception, human meaning, understanding, tokenizer independence or causality, a circuit, behavior, scale law, tuning effects, architecture generality, or model-population generality.",
